haplo-dialog (1.0.0-8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed the binary package from gtk3dialog to haplo-dialog. The name
    gtk3dialog is not free: BunsenLabs has shipped a package by that exact
    name since July 2025, gtk3dialog 0.1.2-3, in a live APT archive at
    pkg.bunsenlabs.org, maintained by Mick Amadio. Their fork and this one
    both descend from Laszlo Pere's gtkdialog, and they renamed first, in
    November 2024.
  * Why this mattered rather than being a matter of etiquette. Two packages
    carrying the SAME name are not rivals to apt, they are one package in two
    versions, and 1.0.0-7 sorts above 0.1.2-3. Provides/Conflicts/Replaces on
    gtkdialog protected nothing here. A BunsenLabs user who added this archive
    for any other Haplo package would have had their gtk3dialog silently
    replaced by a different program on the next upgrade. That is fixed: the
    names now differ, so Conflicts applies, and apt refuses and explains
    instead of substituting in silence.
  * The command does not move. /usr/bin/gtk3dialog and its /usr/bin/gtkdialog
    compatibility symlink are installed exactly as before, so every existing
    script keeps working; only the package that carries them is renamed.
    Provides: gtk3dialog keeps any dependency on the old name satisfied.
  * The new name is the one the project already used everywhere else: the
    domain is haplo-dialog.fr, the manual page is haplo-dialog-xml(5), the
    README and SECURITY.md say haplo-dialog. The package was named after one
    of its ports rather than after the product, which no longer fits now that
    a GTK4 port exists alongside the GTK3 one.
  * Note: /usr/share/doc/gtk3dialog moves to /usr/share/doc/haplo-dialog.

 -- haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 20:49:05 +0200

gtk3dialog (1.0.0-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New attribute headerbar="yes|no" on <window>: client-side decorations.
    "yes" makes the program draw its own title bar, a GtkHeaderBar carrying
    the window title and a close button, instead of the one the window
    manager would draw. There are now three cases, and they say so: nothing
    means the window manager draws the bar, headerbar="yes" means the program
    draws it, decorated="false" means nobody does.
  * It is off by default on purpose. Haplo ships XFCE, where a client-drawn
    bar stops following the xfwm4 theme and its buttons stop matching every
    other window on the desktop. A script that wants that look asks for it.
  * The attribute is not called "titlebar" for a measured reason: GtkWindow in
    GTK4 has a "titlebar" property of type GtkWidget, and tag_attributes.c
    applies any attribute matching a GObject property, so that name would be
    captured and handed a string where a widget is expected. "headerbar" is
    free on GtkWindow in both GTK3 and GTK4.
  * An unrecognised value is reported and treated as "no". Documented in
    gtk3dialog(1) and haplo-dialog-xml(5), with a 55th XML regression case,
    and checked on screen under xfwm4.

 -- haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 20:42:37 +0200

gtk3dialog (1.0.0-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Attribution. The Wayland anchoring added in 1.0.0-4 is derived from the
    BunsenLabs gtk3dialog fork, which is GPL-2.0-or-later, but only the source
    file said so and it named the project rather than the people. The authors
    are now credited where credit legally travels: debian/copyright gains a
    stanza for src/widget_window.c naming Dima Krasner, who introduced
    layer-shell support there in 2021 (commit 025cc69), and Mick Amadio, who
    extended it with edge anchoring, the exclusive zone and opposite-edge
    anchoring between 2021 and 2024. AUTHORS, AUTHORS.en, LICENCES.md and
    LICENCES.en.md carry the same credit.
  * Attribution, correction. debian/copyright listed only Laszlo Pere for
    Files: *, although Thunor is named in every source header and in AUTHORS.
    Thunor is now listed there too.
  * Attribution, correction. AUTHORS filed https://github.com/01micko/gtkdialog
    under Thunor. That repository is Mick Amadio's, not Thunor's. The link has
    been removed from Thunor's entry and Amadio has his own.
  * New attribute reserve="yes|no" on <window>. By default an anchored surface
    floats over ordinary windows; reserve="yes" enables the layer-shell
    auto exclusive zone, so the compositor keeps the surface's space free.
    That is what a bar wants and what a dock usually does not. It has no
    effect without edge=, and says so. Documented in gtk3dialog(1) and
    haplo-dialog-xml(5), with a 54th XML regression case.

 -- haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:50:48 +0200

gtk3dialog (1.0.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Parser. An empty element body is now accepted where emptiness is a value:
    <label></label>, <default></default>, and the attributed form of <item>.
    Writing <text><label>   </label></text> as a spacer used to fail with
    "syntax error" pointing at the closing tag: the lexer drops whitespace, so
    an all-blank body produces no STRING token, and the grammar had only a
    LABEL STRING ELABEL production. Where an empty body has no meaning the
    error now names its cause instead of the closing tag; <sensitive>,
    <width>, <height>, <input>, <input file>, <output>, <variable> and
    <action> answer "the <variable> element is empty; it requires a name."
  * Wayland anchoring, now verified. The layer-shell anchoring shipped in
    1.0.0-4 has since been exercised under sway 1.12 (wlroots 0.20) on a
    headless 1280x720 output and measured to the pixel: a topstride bar flush
    across the full width, a bottom dock exactly dist= pixels off the edge, a
    background strip entirely covered by an ordinary window, and dist=0
    against dist=60 separated by exactly 60 px. The 1.0.0-4 package predates
    that check. Not covered: multi-output, real hardware, and compositors
    outside wlroots such as Hyprland.
  * Note that a bar does not reserve screen space: the exclusive zone is left
    at zero, so an anchored surface floats over ordinary windows rather than
    pushing them aside.
  * Like 1.0.0-4, and unlike 1.0.0-2 and 1.0.0-3, this revision changes the
    binary.

 -- haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:11:53 +0200

gtk3dialog (1.0.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Wayland anchoring. <window> now accepts three attributes, layer=, edge=
    and dist=, which turn the dialog into a wlr-layer-shell surface: a bar, a
    dock, a desktop widget. Ported from the BunsenLabs gtk3dialog fork
    (GPL-2+) with two corrections to the original code:
    - the dist= margin was parsed into an unsigned type and then checked with
      "< 0", a test that can never fire, so an out-of-range value wrapped
      around silently instead of falling back to the default; it is now
      parsed with strtol(), rejects trailing garbage and is clamped to
      [0, 200];
    - the Wayland check read the GDK_BACKEND environment variable and
      proceeded whenever it was unset, which is the normal case under X11;
      the library is now asked directly (gtk_layer_is_supported()), so an
      X11 session or a Wayland compositor without the protocol falls back to
      an ordinary window with a single diagnostic instead of a burst of
      CRITICAL warnings from gtk-layer-shell.
  * Build. New optional dependency gtk-layer-shell >= 0.8.0, wired into
    autotools and CMake; ./configure --without-layer-shell builds without it,
    and the three attributes are then ignored at runtime.
  * Documentation. haplo-dialog-xml(5) documents layer=, edge= and dist=;
    examples/layer-shell shows a bar, a dock and a wallpaper strip.
  * Unlike 1.0.0-2 and 1.0.0-3, this revision does change the binary.
  * The anchoring itself has NOT yet been exercised on a real Wayland
    compositor; only the X11 fallback path is verified.

 -- haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:43:05 +0200

